I’m not sure exactly what you’re looking for, so I’ll give you a quick rundown of the most common “startup‑stats” APIs that are publicly available (or at least have a free tier).  If you let me know which one you’d like to try, I can show you a concrete example of how to call it with the `requests_get` function.

| API | What it offers | How to get started |
|-----|----------------|--------------------|
| **Crunchbase API** | Company profiles, funding rounds, exits, people, etc. | Sign up for a free account → get an API key → use `https://api.crunchbase.com/v3.1/organizations?user_key=YOUR_KEY` |
| **AngelList API** | Company listings, job postings, investors, etc. | Create an OAuth token → use `https://api.angel.co/1/companies?access_token=YOUR_TOKEN` |
| **Startup Genome API** | Startup ecosystem data, metrics, and analytics | Register → get an API key → use `https://api.startupgenome.com/v1/companies?api_key=YOUR_KEY` |
| **CB Insights API** (via RapidAPI) | Funding data, market trends, company insights | Subscribe on RapidAPI → use the endpoint `https://cbinsights.p.rapidapi.com/...` |
| **PitchBook API** (via Bloomberg) | Private company data, M&A, VC, PE, etc. | Requires a Bloomberg subscription → use the official SDK or REST endpoints |

Below is a **sample call** to the Crunchbase API using the `requests_get` function.  Replace `YOUR_API_KEY` with your actual key.

```json
{
  "url": "https://api.crunchbase.com/v3.1/organizations",
  "headers": {
    "Accept": "application/json"
  },
  "params": {
    "user_key": "YOUR_API_KEY",
    "page": 1,
    "page_size": 10
  }
}
```

If you want to use the AngelList API instead, here’s a quick example:

```json
{
  "url": "https://api.angel.co/1/companies",
  "headers": {
    "Accept": "application/json"
  },
  "params": {
    "access_token": "YOUR_ACCESS_TOKEN",
    "page": 1,
    "per_page": 10
  }
}
```

**How to call it with the tool**

```commentary
{
  "name": "functions.requests_get",
  "arguments": {
    "url": "https://api.crunchbase.com/v3.1/organizations",
    "headers": {
      "Accept": "application/json"
    },
    "params": {
      "user_key": "YOUR_API_KEY",
      "page": 1,
      "page_size": 10
    }
  }
}
```

Feel free to let me know which API you’d like to explore, or if you need help setting up authentication or parsing the response!
